WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:02.531
Step back from a mirror.

00:02.970 --> 00:04.710
Do you see MORE of yourself?

00:05.550 --> 00:06.980
You don't.

00:07.000 --> 00:10.466
To see yourself head to toe, you need a mirror half your

00:10.486 --> 00:12.396
height at any distance.

00:14.220 --> 00:17.868
Now, a convex lens forms an image on a screen.

00:18.540 --> 00:20.719
Cover the top half of the lens.

00:21.780 --> 00:23.942
Does half the image disappear?

00:24.410 --> 00:27.847
No! Every part of the lens makes the WHOLE image.

00:27.867 --> 00:29.403
It just gets dimmer.

00:31.076 --> 00:32.495
Take the screen away…

00:32.515 --> 00:34.195
and the rays still meet.

00:34.215 --> 00:36.685
A real image doesn't need a screen.

00:37.589 --> 00:40.690
Finally, shine a laser up out of glass.

00:42.309 --> 00:44.398
Tilt it past forty-two degrees…

00:44.418 --> 00:46.319
and it can't escape.

00:48.169 --> 00:50.433
That's total internal reflection!

00:50.453 --> 00:53.683
It only happens going from glass into air.

00:54.549 --> 00:59.409
LearnLoop AI. Predict. Watch. Explain.
